{"author":{"id":"8d7a7fea5b07a0d5d081edd516d55afeb51ce9c18b2b2be6ceb30eb17cd9b547"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794268271,"nonce":"ejDn6hh6ps7OgKHrF1PSePZQC7g=","message":"PR 71 reworked after the review: the restyle now follows the nodes the incremental update replaced, not the tree.\n\nHow: update_render_props_in_place(_boxed) keeps a node's props when its own hash is unchanged, and queues the node when it replaces them. RenderTree::restyle_replaced_nodes restyles the queued nodes (class, complex and ID rules, Stateful base props, dynamic classes, inherited text from the parent). The desktop runner calls it for VisualOnly and LayoutChanged, the web runner for VisualOnly.\n\nMeasurement (release, this machine, blinc_cn CN_STYLES, rows of card + text + badge + button + checkbox + switch, VisualOnly update changing one colour, mean of 40):\nnodes 151: update 0.38 ms | + full apply_stylesheet_base_styles 1.18 ms | + restyle_replaced_nodes 0.43 ms\nnodes 751: update 1.94 ms | + full 5.77 ms | + replaced 1.99 ms\nnodes 3001: update 8.12 ms | + full 24.20 ms | + replaced 8.47 ms\n(Darmie measured 153/753/3003 nodes: 0.85/4.3/17.6 ms update, 2.6/13.4/55.0 ms with the full pass; his machine is slower, the ratio is the same, about 3x before and about 1.05x after.)\n\nTests: blinc_layout 583 pass, including two new ones (restyle_replaced_nodes only visits replaced nodes; a replaced node takes its class style again). The three blinc_app tests were adapted to the new signature but could not be run here: blinc_app dev-deps pull blinc_media -\u003e alsa-sys, alsa-devel is not installed. blinc_app builds (cargo check). The web.rs change was not compiled (no wasm32 target here).","files":null}]}